      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "An arithmetic sequence $f(n)$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf(n+1)=f(n)+5,\\,f(1)=-21,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nWhat is the $5$th term of the sequence?",
      "worked_solution": "Starting with the first term $f(1)=-21,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive rule until we reach the $5$th term $f(5).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =-21 \\\\ f(2) & =f(1)+5=-21+5=-16 \\\\ f(3) & =f(2)+5=-16+5=-11 \\\\ f(4) & =f(3)+5=-11+5=-6 \\\\ f(5) & =f(4)+5=-6+5=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $5$th term is $f(5)=-1.$",
